    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Traditionalist theologians argue that marriage is a sacred, divinely ordained institution designed specifically for the union of one man and one woman, and they view recent shifts as a dangerous erosion of moral order that undermines human dignity. Their core moral reasoning rests on the belief that nature and scripture reveal an unchangeable truth about human sexuality and procreation, which modern culture has corrupted by prioritizing individual autonomy over communal responsibility. They contend that redefining marriage to include same-sex unions or to separate sex from reproduction destroys the very foundation of the family, leading to societal fragmentation and the loss of shared values. Ultimately, they see the defense of traditional marriage not as exclusion, but as a necessary act of preserving the moral fabric that allows society to flourish.",
