      "content": "it's interesting how they use such heavy language like \"moral decay\" and \"assault\" on human nature. it almost makes it sound like there's no real argument to be made for the other side, like the changes are just objectively bad for civilization. do these theologians think there's any valid way to justify these modern shifts, or do they see the contemporary view as just fundamentally empty of any moral weight?",
